  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth Ambassador SRHR 2025-2027</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The YASRHR program provides a safe and structured space for young people to be meaningfully and inclusively included when it comes to policies on SRHR. The intended end result of the program is as follows:&#x202f; &#x201c;Through the work of the YASRHR, young people are given an official voice in promoting SRHR policy in the Netherlands and globally through empowering young people to become leaders and advocates of SRHR around the world&#x201d;.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The role of Youth Ambassador SRHR, Gender Equality and Bodily Autonomy was set up by the Dutch Ministry of Foreign Affairs (MOFA) and CHOICE for Youth &amp; Sexuality in 2015. Through this program, the MoFA and CHOICE, work together to give young people a voice and a platform to advocate for their sexual and reproductive health and rights (SRHR) and their meaningful and inclusive participation in all areas of decision-making; at the national, regional and international level. This partnership contributes to the development of progressive and inclusive policies for young people and emphasizes the importance of meaningful and inclusive youth participation in the design, development and implementation of sexual health policies. The YASRHR represents a crucial link between young people and the departments that focus on international cooperation of the Dutch Ministry of Foreign Affairs (MoFA) to ensure that their work is in line with the realities of young people. By creating effective channels of collaboration and information exchange, the YASRHR enables policies to be more reflective of the realities of young people so that the solutions brought by these policies adequately represent their needs.</narrative>
  </description>
