  <sector code="13081" percentage="100" vocabulary="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In a time where global public health is a major concern, it is even more evident that SRHR, gender equality and bodily autonomy are essential human rights and need to be treated as such. Youth, minorities and displaced persons most often have the least access to fulfilling their SRH, through inaccessible services, education, or lack of decent work. In response to the visible regressive trend and shrinking civic space, MoFA and YASRHR emphasize the necessity of continued promotion of SRHR, gender equality and bodily autonomy.</narrative>
  </sector>
